      "id": "sol.amc-8-1988-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Each fraction equals \\(\\dfrac{1}{10} = 0.1,\\) since \\(\\dfrac{2}{20} = \\dfrac{3}{30} = \\dfrac{1}{10}.\\)\n\nSo the sum is \\(0.1 + 0.1 + 0.1 = 0.3.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D .",
      "hints": [
        "Each fraction reduces to the same value",
        "\\(\\dfrac{2}{20} = \\dfrac{1}{10}\\) and \\(\\dfrac{3}{30} = \\dfrac{1}{10}\\)"
